name c01m06-thirsty-werewolves
timeout 600
time 1992-10-29T07:48:00Z

# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL (NovaLogic 1992), CAMPAIGN ONE "OPERATION MAXIMUM OVERKILL",
# MISSION 6 OF 10 -- {Thirsty Werewolves}* [MIS].
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/comanche/doc/campaign.md, terrain.md,
# substitutions.md, hud.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [MIS]: 4 fuel depots out of 29 objects, alone, with 14 Werewolves and 11 T-80s in the
# way. The four depots each carry a reinforcement wave at ticks 3 600 / 5 400 / 6 300 / 7 200, rising
# with range from the start (campaign.md 7).
#
# THE FIELD [MIS]: map 4 (Khash Rud, Afghanistan, terrain.md 6), day -- sun +44.47 deg at the
# lead's spawn, computed by the runner. 4 starred objects, unlock marker *.
# THE CAST: 14 Werewolf -> `ah64` - 11 T-80 -> `target_hard` - 4 fuel tank -> `target_soft`.
# THE LOADOUT [MIS]: cannon 500, rockets 62, Hellfire 8, Stinger 8, artillery 4, wingman 0, fuel
# 10800. Declared here: 4 x `mk82`, 4 x `aim9`, gun 500, `set fuel_int_pct 54` = 10800 against the
# campaign's own maximum of 20 000. The rockets and the artillery have no row and no mechanism;
# the truncation of the other two is the F-16's nine pylons.

# ---- THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES ARE STATED IN FULL IN c01m01-werewolves-on-patrol.fbm AND APPLY HERE
# ---- UNCHANGED: D1 no rotorcraft (the RAH-66 flies as `module f16`, 300 kt because 180-275 kt crash
# ---- the egress) - D2 the Werewolf is an `ah64` mover and fires nothing, ever - D3 flat 0 m ground,
# ---- because one mod carries one DEM and this campaign needs four theatres - D4 the clock is checked
# ---- against the logged sun elevation - D5 the anchoring is terrain.md's reconstruction and the
# ---- campaign names no place - D6 the striker spawns on the bearing to its aim point, because the
# ---- attack phase cannot fly itself onto its own run-in - D7 one striker is one aim point.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `lead`'s.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires the 4 fuel depots. The reinforcement waves at ticks 3 600-7 200 mean that
#   in the ORIGINAL a slow run meets an enemy a fast run never sees, so the same rule produces two
#   different fights and both must be reproducible. MEASURED: neither is. `.fbm` is not a schedule
#   (D7's last paragraph), so all 29 objects stand at t = 0 and the two fights collapse into one.
#   exit 3 = the expected reading; report the met count against 4.

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`): ONE OF FOUR.
#   t = 21.4 s          one Mk-82 away, aimErrM 4.39; f01 destroyed
#   verdict             `lead` TIMEOUT, 1 of 4 met, `survive` met. No SAM in this mission. 14
#                       Werewolves and 11 T-80s present from t = 0 and none of them acts.

unit lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight m06 1
  spawn 31.79629 62.92791 150 93.2 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 54
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 4 mk82
  set store 6 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 8 aim9
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 500
  set cmds_mode auto
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 31.79386 62.97916 150 300
  wp 31.79215 63.01512 1000 300
  objective kill unit f01
  objective kill unit f02
  objective kill unit f03
  objective kill unit f04
  objective survive

